          "an asphalt shingle roof typically costs between $10,000 and $18,000, while a metal roof ranges from $15,000 to $48,000"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Cost Breakdown in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "For an average 2,500-square-foot home (about 25 roofing squares):"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Asphalt Shingles:",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Standard Architectural: $12,500 to $18,000 installed."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Class 4 Impact-Resistant: $14,000 to $22,000 installed (often recommended in Utah for hail and severe weather)."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Lifespan: 20 to 30 years."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal Roofing:",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Stone-Coated Steel / Metal Shingles: $22,000 to $40,000 installed."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Standing-Seam Metal (24 gauge): $25,000 to $48,000 installed."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Lifespan: 40 to 70+ years."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Factors to Consider in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Upfront vs. Long-Term Value: Asphalt wins on initial budget. However, because metal lasts twice as long, it often equals or beats asphalt in cost-per-year if you plan to stay in your home long-term."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Weather Performance: Metal handles heavy Utah snow loads by shedding accumulation efficiently and resists high winds and UV rays well. Impact-resistant asphalt handles heavy hail well and is easier to repair."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Complexity: Steeper pitches, valleys, and dormers increase labor costs significantly, especially for specialized standing-seam metal systems."
          }
        ]
      },
